1. Scope and license map

MADI3D uses a mixed licensing model.

Unless a file or component is expressly identified as open-source or
third-party material, MADI3D source code, official executable releases,
documentation, and project-owned assets are governed by the proprietary terms
in this license.

Selected reusable scientific components are separately offered under the GNU
Affero General Public License version 3 only (AGPL-3.0-only). The authoritative
scope of that grant is listed in OpenSource/README.md, and the AGPL license text
is provided in OpenSource/LICENSE.

Third-party software, libraries, data, icons, codecs, templates, and other
components remain governed by their own licenses and notices. Nothing in this
license overrides rights or obligations imposed by those third-party licenses.

If a file-specific license or SPDX notice conflicts with this license, the
file-specific notice controls for that file.

2. Free right to use official MADI3D binary releases

Subject to the proprietary terms below, the copyright holders grant each
recipient a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free right to install and use
unmodified official MADI3D binary releases for any lawful purpose, including
personal, academic, educational, nonprofit, governmental, research, and
commercial internal use.

A user may install MADI3D on multiple devices under that user's control. An
organization may make reasonable copies of an official unmodified binary for
internal deployment within the same legal entity.

MADI3D places no claim on data processed with the software or on scientific
results, figures, screenshots, videos, measurements, analyses, or other output
created by a user with the software.

3. Open-source scientific components

The project may publish scientific algorithms and reusable scientific
infrastructure when doing so directly benefits research and the wider
scientific community.

The initial open-source scope includes the project-owned registration,
stitching, volumetric segmentation, and volume-rendering components identified
in OpenSource/README.md.

Those components are licensed to recipients under AGPL-3.0-only. The AGPL
permits use, study, modification, redistribution, and commercial activity,
including charging for copies or services, subject to its source-availability,
copyleft, notice, and network-interaction requirements. No additional
non-commercial or no-sale restriction is imposed on the AGPL-covered
components.

The MADI3D project may also use the same components in official proprietary
MADI3D releases under separate rights held by, assigned to, or licensed to the
project. This dual-licensing arrangement does not grant recipients a
proprietary license to the AGPL-covered source.

A private development checkout is not by itself a public source release.
Public distribution of an AGPL-covered component must include the applicable
source and license information required by the AGPL.

4. Proprietary MADI3D source code

Except for files expressly covered by OpenSource/README.md or by another
open-source or third-party license, no public source-code license is granted.

Private source access may be provided to approved contributors or collaborators
under separate written authorization and the applicable contributor agreement.
Access to proprietary source code does not grant a right to publish,
redistribute, sublicense, disclose, or make that source code available to any
third party.

