(b) sell, rent, sublicense, repackage, or commercially redistribute the
    proprietary MADI3D application;
(c) provide the proprietary MADI3D application itself, or substantial
    interactive access to its proprietary functionality, as a paid hosted or
    managed software service for third parties without prior written
    permission;
(d) modify, adapt, translate, reverse engineer, decompile, or disassemble
    proprietary MADI3D binaries;
(e) remove or alter copyright, licensing, attribution, or proprietary notices;
(f) use the MADI3D name or logo to imply endorsement, affiliation, or an
    official derivative product without prior written permission.

These restrictions do not limit rights granted under AGPL-3.0-only or another
applicable license for separately licensed components, and do not limit rights
that cannot lawfully be restricted in the user's jurisdiction.

